/-!
# Conformance of the annotated semantics with ProvSQL

The queries of the plain conformance suite (`Provenance.Conformance`), each
with the term written there, and the theorem that the annotated semantics
gives on every instance the annotations ProvSQL gave, over the counting
semiring and over the Boolean semiring under two valuations of the rows.
ProvSQL's answers are in `Provenance.Conformance.ExpectedAnn`, which
`scripts/conformance_ann.py` generates; the modules `Ann.F0` to `Ann.F9`,
one per level of the plain suite, are generated by
`scripts/conformance_ann_lean.py`.

The queries ProvSQL refuses or does not track are left out, with the reason
in `ExpectedAnn`; the warnings it gives on a query it answers are in the
documentation of its answers there.

This is a library of its own, `ConformanceAnn`, outside the default target:
its proofs evaluate every query on every instance in the kernel, which takes
a few minutes and up to 4 GB a module. Each module imports the one before,
so that Lake checks them one at a time, and checks its theorems one at a
time. Build it with
`lake build ConformanceAnn`.
-/
